Blocking findings

1. Cross-version ownership/contract collision. V0.3 makes W4-C own the public MCP tool, taxonomy/grants, schema, receipt, and `tool_placement.rs` surface (`L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:16`, `:69`, `:110`, `:137`, `:172`, `:450`). But v1.4.7 still assigns `dailyos.write.place_document` MCP exposure and `src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/handlers/tool_placement.rs` to W3-B/DOS-480 as a thin wrapper over the v1.4.5 ability, returning `PlaceDocumentReceipt v1` unchanged (`.docs/plans/v1.4.7-waves.md:595`, `:598`, `:599`, `:607`). The v1.4.5 wave plan also says W4-C must not touch v1.4.7 MCP Server v2 tooling (`.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:958`, `:962`, `:963`). Action: either amend both wave plans to transfer MCP handler/taxonomy/grant/error/receipt ownership into W4-C, or narrow W4-C back to ability/service/allowlist and leave public MCP exposure to DOS-480. Sync ability name, request, receipt, idempotency, and error shapes in the same amendment.

2. Conversation-handle transport gap. V0.3 treats placement as conversation-aware (`L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:25`, `:200`, `:290`) and v1.4.7 requires first-write handle return/cross-conversation continuity (`.docs/plans/v1.4.7-waves.md:606`, `:700`). Live rmcp transport always builds requests with `conversation_handle: None` (`src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/transport.rs:173`) and discards `McpToolResponseEnvelope.conversation_handle` when returning `Content::text` (`src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/transport.rs:207`). Gateway mints rows, but clients cannot receive or echo handles. Action: block W4-C MCP exposure until a transport amendment or PR #355 explicitly round-trips `conversation_handle` over rmcp with golden wire tests, or remove conversation-handle-dependent semantics and v1.4.7 compatibility claims from W4-C.

Final verdict: HOLD.